course: dictionary
lesson: 11886
title: Brethren: family in faith
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Brethren is an old word. It is the plural of brother, but it is used in a more formal way. When you meet a hard word, look at the words around it. «Dearly beloved brethren, let us pray» is said in a church, so the clues point to church members.
explain: Brethren means fellow members of a church or group. It can also mean brothers, in very old or formal language. When the speaker says brethren, they are talking to people as if they were family.
explain: Read the clues: church, hymn, Bible and chapel all tell you that brethren is about religious groups. Try your meaning in the sentence. «The brethren sang the old hymn» still makes sense if brethren means fellow church members.
fact: Brethren is the old plural of brother.
fact: Brethren can mean fellow members of a church or religious group.
fact: In old or formal language, brethren can mean brothers.
fact: Brethren is also used for members of the same group or profession, such as «brethren in the same trade».
fact: Some church groups call themselves the Brethren, with a capital B.
exercise: «The minister said, "Dearly beloved brethren, let us pray."» Who is the minister speaking to? | *Fellow members of the church | Football fans in the stadium | Children in a school playground | Farmers at the market
exercise: «The old hymn was sung by the brethren in the chapel.» What are the brethren? | Shopkeepers | *Members of the same church group | Sailors on a ship | Pilots flying a plane
exercise: «They called each other brethren, like family in faith.» What does brethren show? | The speakers are hungry | *The speakers see each other as family in faith | The speakers are angry at each other | The speakers are lost
test: «Brethren in Christ» means which of these? | Musicians in a band | Strangers who have just met | *Fellow believers in Christ | Brothers who work in shops
test: Ella says brethren is just a fancy word for friends. What is the best reply? | Yes, it means exactly the same as friends | *Not quite: it suggests fellow members of a group, with a feeling of family | No, it means people who are very tall | No, it means nothing at all
exam: Which clue in a sentence helps you know brethren means church members? | The word has two syllables | The sentence ends with a question mark | The word is written in capital letters | *Words like church, hymn or Bible nearby
